From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Romeu Mello <romeumello@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:51:54 -0300
Subject: unix-half-close: the unix proxy carries the host's half-close to the guest as one

## Why virtx needs it

A published port reaches the guest through a unix socket libkrun listens on (`add_unix_port`), relayed from the port's listener by virtx-uvm/src/machine/net/relay.rs.
Upstream answers the host's EOF on that socket with a reset, so a client that sends its request and shuts down its write side never hears the answer.
virtx-rs/tests/ports.rs `a_port_carries_a_half_close_through` fails without it.

## What it changes

libkrun#973 (https://github.com/libkrun/libkrun/pull/973), its commit as it is, less the test it adds to libkrun's own suite.
The host's EOF becomes a send-only vsock shutdown, ordered after the data already pushed; the guest's shutdown reaches the host socket one direction at a time; on macOS an accepted socket gets `SO_NOSIGPIPE`, since the guest may now write after the host side is gone.

## When it can go

When libkrun#973 is merged.
